Subject: Poll the interrupt handler on every compiled back edge

What this does
  `qjs_aot_poll` decrements the context's interrupt counter and runs the
  embedder's handler at zero, the same poll an interpreter back edge runs. The
  generator emits it on every backward branch, including the back edge of a
  typed loop region, whose body is a tight native loop with nothing else in it.

Why we need it
  `JS_SetInterruptHandler` is how an embedder stops runaway script (the React
  Native watchdog), and patch 0213 made every interpreter back edge poll it. A
  compiled loop that neither allocates nor calls -- `while (true) {}`, or a
  numeric loop lowered to a typed region -- had no poll, so it could not be
  stopped. That is the loophole the design names in 6.8.

What it adds
  `qjs_aot_poll` in the engine and its declaration, and the poll at every
  backward branch and region back edge in the generator.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs-aot-rt.h b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
